WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.688
The kit's definition is the
one every integration deploys.

2
00:00:03.688 --> 00:00:07.751
What changes between integrations
is data: four parameters,

3
00:00:07.751 --> 00:00:12.463
the Graph host, the downstream system,
its audience, and the operations.

4
00:00:12.463 --> 00:00:14.338
A run goes in four steps.

5
00:00:14.338 --> 00:00:18.435
Check request checks that the callback
path is a resume path for this

6
00:00:18.435 --> 00:00:22.676
workflow and this task processing
result, and that the subject has an I D.

7
00:00:22.676 --> 00:00:27.625
If not, the run stops and sends nothing,
because it can't trust the path.

8
00:00:27.625 --> 00:00:32.138
Operation looks up the workflow; an
unregistered one gets no work done.

9
00:00:32.138 --> 00:00:37.005
Call integration posts to the downstream
system with an idempotency key,

10
00:00:37.005 --> 00:00:39.000
the task processing result I D.

11
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.636
The key is the kit's design,

12
00:00:40.636 --> 00:00:44.688
a contract with the downstream
system, not a Microsoft feature.

13
00:00:44.688 --> 00:00:47.748
It retries transient
errors up to four times,

14
00:00:47.748 --> 00:00:52.876
with a retry policy from Learn's page
on handling errors in Azure Logic Apps.

15
00:00:52.876 --> 00:00:57.071
And Resume posts to the Graph
host on v1.0, after success,

16
00:00:57.071 --> 00:01:02.387
failure or time-out, and reports
completed only if the call succeeded.

17
00:01:02.387 --> 00:01:05.308
The registry holds one
entry per integration,

18
00:01:05.308 --> 00:01:10.300
and the builder refuses values outside
the ranges in Learn's Graph reference.
